nc ParseLLMFingerprint(fp string) (rule, path, symbol string, ok bool)\n```\n- `path` must also appear in `f.Files`. `exists` is injected so that the test needs no worktree. PR 2 passes an `os.Root`-based `Lstat` on the read-only worktree, which never follows a symlink out.\n\n**`internal/scanner/neardup.go`** (new, pure)\n```go\n// NearDupThreshold is the Jaccard similarity of two titles' word sets at or\n// above which they are near-duplicates.\nconst NearDupThreshold = 0.8\n\n// TitledIssue is an open issue of the scanner: its title and every checklist line title.\ntype TitledIssue struct {\n\tNumber int\n\tTitles []string\n}\n\n// NearDup is a finding skipped because its title matches Issue (0 = an\n// earlier finding of the same run).\ntype NearDup struct {\n\tFingerprint string\n\tIssue       int\n}\n\n// SimilarTitles: lowercase; every rune outside [a-z0-9] becomes a space;\n// drop one-character tokens and a fixed stop list (a an and for in is of on\n// the to with); compare as sets. Equal non-empty sets are similar. Otherwise\n// both need at least 3 tokens and Jaccard >= NearDupThreshold.\nfunc SimilarTitles(a, b string) bool\n\n// SkipNearDuplicates walks items in the given order (most severe first, as\n// sortedItems returns) and drops an item whose title is similar to any open\n// issue's titles or to an item already kept.\nfunc SkipNearDuplicates(items []Item, open []TitledIssue) (kept []Item, dups []NearDup)\n```\n\n**`internal/scanner/pipeline.go`**\n- `IssueView` gains `Title string`, filled from `github.Issue.Title` where views are built.\n- In `Run`, after `items` is built and before `PlanGroups`: if `role.LLMScanner()`, sort the items by severity rank, descending, then by fingerprint. Build `[]TitledIssue` from the views (`v.Title` plus `v.Parsed.Lines[i].Title`), call `SkipNearDuplicates`, and log one `scanner.near_duplicate` per skip (`fingerprint`, `issue`).\n- `RunResult` gains `NearDup int`, which the `scanner.run` log carries as `near_dupli